    "compiledPromptMd": "# SCION MULTI-SWARM \u00b7 #02 (#02 \u00b7 Galley \u2014 Diner window: Trout Cook with silver baster)\n\nLineage: TROUTOWN Ep. 5 (Something in the Kitchen) \u00b7 BOLAS Register: `queneau-rostrum` (Queneau Rostrum Cutout) \u00b7 Workshop: Oubapo \u00b7 Director Swarm: S11 Connelly Barnes \u2014 Video Puppetry Tabletop.\n\n## 1. Assignment\nYou are the coordinated 4-SCION autonomous rostrum crew for Turkey Sub Porthole #02 \u00b7 Galley (\u201cDiner window: Trout Cook with silver baster\u201d). Produce a 16.0-second (`384` frames @ `24fps`, `1280\u00d7720`) foraged-plate + split-pin cutout film (`films/portholes/p02.mp4`) and live 60fps playable rig (`window.PORTAL_REMAKE_SCENES[2]`) in the authentic BOLAS Oulipo Screening Room aesthetic (`queneau-rostrum`, inspired by `exercices-de-style.webp (Raymond Queneau \u00b7 1947)`).\n\n## 2. Creative Thesis\n\u201cForaged or handmade, never faked.\u201d Repeat one drawing nine times and let two traversal orders change what its captions mean. Oubapo dual-caption rostrum: on buttercream paper beside a torn-deckle service window, keep the silver baster cutout constant while re-staging 4 incompatible kitchen/submarine/cosmic operations.\nRostrum Materiality (`queneau-rostrum`): Warm buttercream/ochre rostrum paper, white-halo scissor-cut plate crops, torn-deckle architectural flats, and a 4-box contact filmstrip tracker with stamp-red active border.\n\n## 3. Active SCION Swarm Stack (4 Swarms + 2 Real Plates)\n- **Foraged Plates:** `./portholes/p02.jpg` + `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-47.webp` (Something in the Kitchen \u00b7 Corridor. A resident in work clothes stands near the camera with a fluorescent corridor and another figure behind.), preloaded via `SCION_STAGE.preloadPortalPlates(2)` and sliced via `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`.\n1. **Ouxpo / Oulipo Workshop SCION \u2014 Oubapo (One image, two orders of captions):** Ouvroir de bande dessin\u00e9e potentielle \u00b7 Comics. Rule: Repeat one drawing nine times and let two traversal orders change what its captions mean. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/oubapo/)\n2. **Director / Artistic Lineage Swarm \u2014 S11 Connelly Barnes \u2014 Video Puppetry Tabletop:** Video Puppetry: A Performative Interface for Cutout Animation (2008); coauthors Jacobs, Sanders, Goldman, Rusinkiewicz, Finkelstein and Agrawala. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s11)\n3. **Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Tech Swarms:**\n   - **S33 Inverse Kinematics \u2014 Contact and Reach Swarm:** 2-bone IK split-pin trout-cook arm & baster (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s33)\n   - **S43 Collage Graph Rewriting \u2014 Identity Change Swarm:** Rostrum cutout swap: baster -> air pump -> roast -> warp syringe (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s43)\n   - **S47 Sound-to-Action \u2014 Viseme and Gesture Swarm:** Bulb-squeeze synced to percussive foley (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s47)\n4. **Turkey Sub World Atlas SCION \u2014 Something in the Kitchen (`#film-_yzBmbqP6vk`):** \u201cCarry one object from counter to boat\u201d (./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-_yzBmbqP6vk)\n\n## 4. 4-Beat Cutaway Invariants (A\u00b7B\u00b7C\u00b7D \u00b7 16.0s + Snail Mail)\n- **Variation I (`0.0\u20134.0s` \u00b7 A \u00b7 Real Creek \u00b7 `#14110d`):** Stage **\u201cTrout Cook holding a silver baster\u201d** from scissor-cut real plate fragments and torn-paper flats.\n- **Variation II (`4.0\u20138.0s` \u00b7 B \u00b7 Probable (Turkey) \u00b7 `#1d596e`):** Rostrum shutter cut! Reframe the silhouette with split-pin cardboard/litho pieces into **\u201cA friendly submarine air pump\u201d** as Turkey\u2019s wing dispatches the **Mail Snail** with a wax-sealed postcard.\n- **Variation III (`8.0\u201312.0s` \u00b7 C \u00b7 Plausible (Trout) \u00b7 `#0f8f80`):** Creek witness cut! Brook the Trout inspects the scene reframed as **\u201cA canned roast dinner delivery\u201d**, stamping the green reply as Mail Snail climbs the right edge.\n- **Variation IV (`12.0\u201316.0s` \u00b7 D \u00b7 Preposterous (Alien) \u00b7 `#d42a1e`):** Cosmic listening-post cut! The 3-eyed **Alien Listener** saucer scans and re-stages the cutouts into **\u201cA warp-core fuel syringe\u201d**.\n\n## 5. Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Rig\n- Combine `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`, `SCION_STAGE.drawTornPaperFlat`, `SCION_STAGE.drawCardboardPuppetPiece`, `SCION_STAGE.drawSplitPin`, `SCION_STAGE.solveIK2`, and `SCION_STAGE.spring`.\n- Bind interactive 60fps state: `state.lamp`, `state.ballast`, `state.snailActive`/`state.snailT`, `state.roll` (1\u20136 die pips), and `state.view` (`\"real\" | \"turkey\" | \"trout\" | \"alien\" | \"auto\"`).\n- Mix 16.0s 44.1kHz stereo audio: dry spoken art-house variation cues (`Moira` @ -16 dBFS) + paper slide, scissor snip, split-pin creak, postal bell, water lap, and Beat IV listening-post tone (`RMS > 0.025`).\n\n## 6. Hard Proof (16.0s / 384f)\n- Render `films/portholes/p02.mp4` (`1280x720`, `24fps`, `384` frames, `-crf 22`, AAC stereo), blind poster `thumbs/p02-remake.jpg` (`t = 2.2s`, `showCaptions: false`), and 4-column strip `checks/p02-remake-strip.jpg` (`2.0s, 6.0s, 10.0s, 14.0s`).\n- Provenance summary (8 sources): A 16.0-second (384-frame) four-variation cutout film in the Queneau Rostrum Cutout register, after TROUTOWN Ep. 5 (Something in the Kitchen) and Oubapo (Ouvroir de bande dessin\u00e9e potentielle \u00b7 Comics). Foraged: porthole plate ./portholes/p02.jpg and Interior Atlas frame ./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-47.webp (\u201cSomething in the Kitchen \u00b7 Corridor. A resident in work clothes stands near the camera with a fluorescent corridor and another figure behind.\u201d), sliced in code into irregular scissor-halo cutouts and multiplane depth cards\u2014never shown as a flat full-frame slide. Handmade: articulated grey-cardboard and deckle-paper pieces with metallic split-pin brads (S33/S43), staging all four student readings\u2014(A) \u201cTrout Cook holding a silver baster\u201d, (B) \u201cA friendly submarine air pump\u201d with Snail Mail dispatch, (C) \u201cA canned roast dinner delivery\u201d with Brook Trout's reply, and (D) \u201cA warp-core fuel syringe\u201d under the Alien Listening Post. Sound: dry documentary voiceover (Moira, -16 dBFS) paired with synthesized paper rustle, split-pin creak, brass postal chime, river lap, and listening-post tone, with declared quiet intervals between cuts.\n\n## 7. Blind Critic Fixture\n- **PAELEO Hard Invariant:** When `state.showCaptions === false`, emit **ZERO** `ctx.fillText` or `ctx.strokeText` calls anywhere (`0` leaked characters). Delegate all captions and the 4-box contact filmstrip to `SCION_STAGE.drawBolasSlateAndStrip` / `SCION_STAGE.drawRubricBar`.\n- Independent critic inspects `checks/p02-remake-strip.jpg` against `/tmp/bolas_refs/*.webp` and `./portholes/p02.jpg` to verify tactile cut-paper/cardboard/lithograph craft and distinct 4-beat visual transformations.\n\n## 8. Repair Loop\n- Reject flat untextured cartoon shapes or static Ken-Burns slides; re-cut plate fragments into articulated multi-plane pieces with visible paper halos, charcoal shading, and split-pin joints.\n\n## 9. Source Anchors\n- Porthole Plate: `./portholes/p02.jpg` \u00b7 Atlas Still: `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-47.webp` ([source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_yzBmbqP6vk&t=22s))\n- BOLAS Screening Room: [Oulipo Screening Room](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/screening/)\n- Workshop SCION: [Oubapo](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/oubapo/) \u00b7 Director Swarm: [S11 Connelly Barnes \u2014 Video Puppetry Tabletop](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s11)\n- Tech Swarms: [S33](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s33) \u00b7 [S43](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s43) \u00b7 [S47](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s47) \u00b7 Atlas: [Something in the Kitchen](./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-_yzBmbqP6vk)",
    "compiledPromptPoml": ""
