    "compiledPromptMd": "# SCION MULTI-SWARM \u00b7 #03 (#03 \u00b7 Starbd \u2014 Room 4 chalkboard listing HOOK MONSTER)\n\nLineage: TROUTOWN Ep. 2 (The School of Fish) \u00b7 BOLAS Register: `perec-stage` (Carved Paper Proscenium & Tinted Archive) \u00b7 Workshop: Outypopo \u00b7 Director Swarm: S17 South Park \u2014 Repeatable Graphic Grammar.\n\n## 1. Assignment\nYou are the coordinated 4-SCION autonomous rostrum crew for Turkey Sub Porthole #03 \u00b7 Starbd (\u201cRoom 4 chalkboard listing HOOK MONSTER\u201d). Produce a 16.0-second (`384` frames @ `24fps`, `1280\u00d7720`) foraged-plate + split-pin cutout film (`films/portholes/p03.mp4`) and live 60fps playable rig (`window.PORTAL_REMAKE_SCENES[3]`) in the authentic BOLAS Oulipo Screening Room aesthetic (`perec-stage`, inspired by `les-lieux-dune-fugue.webp (Georges Perec \u00b7 1978)`).\n\n## 2. Creative Thesis\n\u201cForaged or handmade, never faked.\u201d Keep a text verbatim and use line breaks to reveal a second reading. Outypopo architectural stage: open carved paper schoolroom doors onto the sunken Room 4 chalkboard plate as it shifts across classroom slate, bandit poster, barbed Hook Monster, and galactic bounty board.\nRostrum Materiality (`perec-stage`): Carved sandstone/ochre paper masonry proscenium with relief shadows and hinged paper shutters opening onto cool cyanotype/sepia archival plates.\n\n## 3. Active SCION Swarm Stack (4 Swarms + 2 Real Plates)\n- **Foraged Plates:** `./portholes/p03.jpg` + `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-49.webp` (The School of Fish \u00b7 Chalkboard wall. An upright trout is framed next to a chalkboard, which holds one readable zone in the room.), preloaded via `SCION_STAGE.preloadPortalPlates(3)` and sliced via `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`.\n1. **Ouxpo / Oulipo Workshop SCION \u2014 Outypopo (An acrostic made with line breaks):** Potential typography \u00b7 Typographic and visual poetry. Rule: Keep a text verbatim and use line breaks to reveal a second reading. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/outypopo/)\n2. **Director / Artistic Lineage Swarm \u2014 S17 South Park \u2014 Repeatable Graphic Grammar:** Paper-cutout look recreated with digital production and reusable character conventions. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s17)\n3. **Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Tech Swarms:**\n   - **S44 Multiplane Parallax \u2014 Spatial Collage Swarm:** Carved classroom masonry proscenium & sunken recess (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s44)\n   - **S39 Multiview Drawing Substitution \u2014 Turn Lab:** 4-variation torn-slate cutout replacement (0 blind text) (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s39)\n   - **S48 State Machines \u2014 Characters That Can Refuse:** Hinged shutter & bounty-grid state machine (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s48)\n4. **Turkey Sub World Atlas SCION \u2014 The School of Fish (`#film-eu0CarKpDLA`):** \u201cTeach a part with a demonstration\u201d (./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-eu0CarKpDLA)\n\n## 4. 4-Beat Cutaway Invariants (A\u00b7B\u00b7C\u00b7D \u00b7 16.0s + Snail Mail)\n- **Variation I (`0.0\u20134.0s` \u00b7 A \u00b7 Real Creek \u00b7 `#14110d`):** Stage **\u201cA sunken Room 4 chalkboard\u201d** from scissor-cut real plate fragments and torn-paper flats.\n- **Variation II (`4.0\u20138.0s` \u00b7 B \u00b7 Probable (Turkey) \u00b7 `#1d596e`):** Rostrum shutter cut! Reframe the silhouette with split-pin cardboard/litho pieces into **\u201cA Most Wanted bandit poster\u201d** as Turkey\u2019s wing dispatches the **Mail Snail** with a wax-sealed postcard.\n- **Variation III (`8.0\u201312.0s` \u00b7 C \u00b7 Plausible (Trout) \u00b7 `#0f8f80`):** Creek witness cut! Brook the Trout inspects the scene reframed as **\u201cThe dreaded creek Hook Monster\u201d**, stamping the green reply as Mail Snail climbs the right edge.\n- **Variation IV (`12.0\u201316.0s` \u00b7 D \u00b7 Preposterous (Alien) \u00b7 `#d42a1e`):** Cosmic listening-post cut! The 3-eyed **Alien Listener** saucer scans and re-stages the cutouts into **\u201cA galactic bounty-hunter board\u201d**.\n\n## 5. Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Rig\n- Combine `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`, `SCION_STAGE.drawTornPaperFlat`, `SCION_STAGE.drawCardboardPuppetPiece`, `SCION_STAGE.drawSplitPin`, `SCION_STAGE.solveIK2`, and `SCION_STAGE.spring`.\n- Bind interactive 60fps state: `state.lamp`, `state.ballast`, `state.snailActive`/`state.snailT`, `state.roll` (1\u20136 die pips), and `state.view` (`\"real\" | \"turkey\" | \"trout\" | \"alien\" | \"auto\"`).\n- Mix 16.0s 44.1kHz stereo audio: dry spoken art-house variation cues (`Samantha` @ -16 dBFS) + paper slide, scissor snip, split-pin creak, postal bell, water lap, and Beat IV listening-post tone (`RMS > 0.025`).\n\n## 6. Hard Proof (16.0s / 384f)\n- Render `films/portholes/p03.mp4` (`1280x720`, `24fps`, `384` frames, `-crf 22`, AAC stereo), blind poster `thumbs/p03-remake.jpg` (`t = 2.2s`, `showCaptions: false`), and 4-column strip `checks/p03-remake-strip.jpg` (`2.0s, 6.0s, 10.0s, 14.0s`).\n- Provenance summary (10 sources): A 16.0-second (384-frame) four-variation cutout film in the Carved Paper Proscenium & Tinted Archive register, after TROUTOWN Ep. 2 (The School of Fish) and Outypopo (Potential typography \u00b7 Typographic and visual poetry). Foraged: porthole plate ./portholes/p03.jpg and Interior Atlas frame ./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-49.webp (\u201cThe School of Fish \u00b7 Chalkboard wall. An upright trout is framed next to a chalkboard, which holds one readable zone in the room.\u201d), sliced in code into irregular scissor-halo cutouts and multiplane depth cards\u2014never shown as a flat full-frame slide. Handmade: articulated grey-cardboard and deckle-paper pieces with metallic split-pin brads (S44/S39), staging all four student readings\u2014(A) \u201cA sunken Room 4 chalkboard\u201d, (B) \u201cA Most Wanted bandit poster\u201d with Snail Mail dispatch, (C) \u201cThe dreaded creek Hook Monster\u201d with Brook Trout's reply, and (D) \u201cA galactic bounty-hunter board\u201d under the Alien Listening Post. Sound: dry documentary voiceover (Samantha, -16 dBFS) paired with synthesized paper rustle, split-pin creak, brass postal chime, river lap, and listening-post tone, with declared quiet intervals between cuts.\n\n## 7. Blind Critic Fixture\n- **PAELEO Hard Invariant:** When `state.showCaptions === false`, emit **ZERO** `ctx.fillText` or `ctx.strokeText` calls anywhere (`0` leaked characters). Delegate all captions and the 4-box contact filmstrip to `SCION_STAGE.drawBolasSlateAndStrip` / `SCION_STAGE.drawRubricBar`.\n- Independent critic inspects `checks/p03-remake-strip.jpg` against `/tmp/bolas_refs/*.webp` and `./portholes/p03.jpg` to verify tactile cut-paper/cardboard/lithograph craft and distinct 4-beat visual transformations.\n\n## 8. Repair Loop\n- Reject flat untextured cartoon shapes or static Ken-Burns slides; re-cut plate fragments into articulated multi-plane pieces with visible paper halos, charcoal shading, and split-pin joints.\n\n## 9. Source Anchors\n- Porthole Plate: `./portholes/p03.jpg` \u00b7 Atlas Still: `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-49.webp` ([source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eu0CarKpDLA&t=24s))\n- BOLAS Screening Room: [Oulipo Screening Room](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/screening/)\n- Workshop SCION: [Outypopo](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/outypopo/) \u00b7 Director Swarm: [S17 South Park \u2014 Repeatable Graphic Grammar](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s17)\n- Tech Swarms: [S44](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s44) \u00b7 [S39](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s39) \u00b7 [S48](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s48) \u00b7 Atlas: [The School of Fish](./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-eu0CarKpDLA)",
    "compiledPromptPoml": ""
