    "compiledPromptMd": "# SCION MULTI-SWARM \u00b7 #12 (#12 \u00b7 Keel \u2014 Cardboard stage with green Floor Porthole)\n\nLineage: Yellow Submarine (1968 \u00b7 Sea of Holes) \u00b7 BOLAS Register: `duchamp-optic` (Engraved Rotor, Paper-Tooth & Reverse-Melt Slate) \u00b7 Workshop: A Morning Stroll \u00b7 Director Swarm: S01 Terry Gilliam \u2014 Comic Cutout Metamorphosis.\n\n## 1. Assignment\nYou are the coordinated 4-SCION autonomous rostrum crew for Turkey Sub Porthole #12 \u00b7 Keel (\u201cCardboard stage with green Floor Porthole\u201d). Produce a 16.0-second (`384` frames @ `24fps`, `1280\u00d7720`) foraged-plate + split-pin cutout film (`films/portholes/p12.mp4`) and live 60fps playable rig (`window.PORTAL_REMAKE_SCENES[12]`) in the authentic BOLAS Oulipo Screening Room aesthetic (`duchamp-optic`, inspired by `anemic-cinema / zazie-dans-le-metro / le-chant-du-styrene`).\n\n## 2. Creative Thesis\n\u201cForaged or handmade, never faked.\u201d Make the same encounter legible as world, medium, and genre change. Sea-of-Holes optical stage: cut a luminous emerald circular aperture into corrugated dark stage board and rotate concentric rings through stage window, whirlpool drain, $1 sideshow spot, and pocket-universe trapdoor.\nRostrum Materiality (`duchamp-optic`): Dark workshop slate stage featuring eccentric engraved optical discs, physical cut-paper block typography/props, or reverse-extrusion runner cutouts with cream scissor halos.\n\n## 3. Active SCION Swarm Stack (4 Swarms + 2 Real Plates)\n- **Foraged Plates:** `./portholes/p12.jpg` + `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-09.webp` (On Melancholy Hill \u00b7 Porthole view of crew. Two drawn faces fit inside the rounded window. The curved frame and dim depth hold the hatch geometry together.), preloaded via `SCION_STAGE.preloadPortalPlates(12)` and sliced via `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`.\n1. **Ouxpo / Oulipo Workshop SCION \u2014 A Morning Stroll (One encounter across three eras):** Grant Orchard \u00b7 Studio AKA \u00b7 2011. Rule: Make the same encounter legible as world, medium, and genre change. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/a-morning-stroll/)\n2. **Director / Artistic Lineage Swarm \u2014 S01 Terry Gilliam \u2014 Comic Cutout Metamorphosis:** 1974 BBC cutout demonstration; Monty Python collage interludes. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s1)\n3. **Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Tech Swarms:**\n   - **S31 Alpha Matting \u2014 Hair, Lace and Smoke Swarm:** Concentric green floor-porthole iris rings (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s31)\n   - **S44 Multiplane Parallax \u2014 Spatial Collage Swarm:** Vertical cardboard rib-zoom parallax (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s44)\n   - **S43 Collage Graph Rewriting \u2014 Identity Change Swarm:** Optical trapdoor swap into whirlpool, spotlight & wormhole (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s43)\n4. **Turkey Sub World Atlas SCION \u2014 On Melancholy Hill (`#film-04mfKJWDSzI`):** \u201cA warm crew behind a cold porthole\u201d (./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-04mfKJWDSzI)\n\n## 4. 4-Beat Cutaway Invariants (A\u00b7B\u00b7C\u00b7D \u00b7 16.0s + Snail Mail)\n- **Variation I (`0.0\u20134.0s` \u00b7 A \u00b7 Real Creek \u00b7 `#14110d`):** Stage **\u201cA cardboard stage floor window\u201d** from scissor-cut real plate fragments and torn-paper flats.\n- **Variation II (`4.0\u20138.0s` \u00b7 B \u00b7 Probable (Turkey) \u00b7 `#1d596e`):** Rostrum shutter cut! Reframe the silhouette with split-pin cardboard/litho pieces into **\u201cA spinning creek whirlpool drain\u201d** as Turkey\u2019s wing dispatches the **Mail Snail** with a wax-sealed postcard.\n- **Variation III (`8.0\u201312.0s` \u00b7 C \u00b7 Plausible (Trout) \u00b7 `#0f8f80`):** Creek witness cut! Brook the Trout inspects the scene reframed as **\u201cA one-dollar sideshow spotlight\u201d**, stamping the green reply as Mail Snail climbs the right edge.\n- **Variation IV (`12.0\u201316.0s` \u00b7 D \u00b7 Preposterous (Alien) \u00b7 `#d42a1e`):** Cosmic listening-post cut! The 3-eyed **Alien Listener** saucer scans and re-stages the cutouts into **\u201cA secret pocket-universe trapdoor\u201d**.\n\n## 5. Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Rig\n- Combine `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`, `SCION_STAGE.drawTornPaperFlat`, `SCION_STAGE.drawCardboardPuppetPiece`, `SCION_STAGE.drawSplitPin`, `SCION_STAGE.solveIK2`, and `SCION_STAGE.spring`.\n- Bind interactive 60fps state: `state.lamp`, `state.ballast`, `state.snailActive`/`state.snailT`, `state.roll` (1\u20136 die pips), and `state.view` (`\"real\" | \"turkey\" | \"trout\" | \"alien\" | \"auto\"`).\n- Mix 16.0s 44.1kHz stereo audio: dry spoken art-house variation cues (`Rishi` @ -16 dBFS) + paper slide, scissor snip, split-pin creak, postal bell, water lap, and Beat IV listening-post tone (`RMS > 0.025`).\n\n## 6. Hard Proof (16.0s / 384f)\n- Render `films/portholes/p12.mp4` (`1280x720`, `24fps`, `384` frames, `-crf 22`, AAC stereo), blind poster `thumbs/p12-remake.jpg` (`t = 2.2s`, `showCaptions: false`), and 4-column strip `checks/p12-remake-strip.jpg` (`2.0s, 6.0s, 10.0s, 14.0s`).\n- Provenance summary (9 sources): A 16.0-second (384-frame) four-variation cutout film in the Engraved Rotor, Paper-Tooth & Reverse-Melt Slate register, after Yellow Submarine (1968 \u00b7 Sea of Holes) and A Morning Stroll (Grant Orchard \u00b7 Studio AKA \u00b7 2011). Foraged: porthole plate ./portholes/p12.jpg and Interior Atlas frame ./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-09.webp (\u201cOn Melancholy Hill \u00b7 Porthole view of crew. Two drawn faces fit inside the rounded window. The curved frame and dim depth hold the hatch geometry together.\u201d), sliced in code into irregular scissor-halo cutouts and multiplane depth cards\u2014never shown as a flat full-frame slide. Handmade: articulated grey-cardboard and deckle-paper pieces with metallic split-pin brads (S31/S44), staging all four student readings\u2014(A) \u201cA cardboard stage floor window\u201d, (B) \u201cA spinning creek whirlpool drain\u201d with Snail Mail dispatch, (C) \u201cA one-dollar sideshow spotlight\u201d with Brook Trout's reply, and (D) \u201cA secret pocket-universe trapdoor\u201d under the Alien Listening Post. Sound: dry documentary voiceover (Rishi, -16 dBFS) paired with synthesized paper rustle, split-pin creak, brass postal chime, river lap, and listening-post tone, with declared quiet intervals between cuts.\n\n## 7. Blind Critic Fixture\n- **PAELEO Hard Invariant:** When `state.showCaptions === false`, emit **ZERO** `ctx.fillText` or `ctx.strokeText` calls anywhere (`0` leaked characters). Delegate all captions and the 4-box contact filmstrip to `SCION_STAGE.drawBolasSlateAndStrip` / `SCION_STAGE.drawRubricBar`.\n- Independent critic inspects `checks/p12-remake-strip.jpg` against `/tmp/bolas_refs/*.webp` and `./portholes/p12.jpg` to verify tactile cut-paper/cardboard/lithograph craft and distinct 4-beat visual transformations.\n\n## 8. Repair Loop\n- Reject flat untextured cartoon shapes or static Ken-Burns slides; re-cut plate fragments into articulated multi-plane pieces with visible paper halos, charcoal shading, and split-pin joints.\n\n## 9. Source Anchors\n- Porthole Plate: `./portholes/p12.jpg` \u00b7 Atlas Still: `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-09.webp` ([source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=04mfKJWDSzI&t=140s))\n- BOLAS Screening Room: [Oulipo Screening Room](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/screening/)\n- Workshop SCION: [A Morning Stroll](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/a-morning-stroll/) \u00b7 Director Swarm: [S01 Terry Gilliam \u2014 Comic Cutout Metamorphosis](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s1)\n- Tech Swarms: [S31](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s31) \u00b7 [S44](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s44) \u00b7 [S43](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s43) \u00b7 Atlas: [On Melancholy Hill](./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-04mfKJWDSzI)",
    "compiledPromptPoml": ""
