    "compiledPromptMd": "# SCION MULTI-SWARM \u00b7 #13 (#13 \u00b7 Arch \u2014 Bell Boulder arch with brass twig-bell)\n\nLineage: TROUTOWN Ep. 3 (Trading on the Current) \u00b7 BOLAS Register: `cardboard-parallax` (Split-Pin Cardboard & Silver-Gelatin Parallax) \u00b7 Workshop: Boucle-l\u00e0 ! \u00b7 Director Swarm: S02 Lotte Reiniger \u2014 Articulated Shadow Theater.\n\n## 1. Assignment\nYou are the coordinated 4-SCION autonomous rostrum crew for Turkey Sub Porthole #13 \u00b7 Arch (\u201cBell Boulder arch with brass twig-bell\u201d). Produce a 16.0-second (`384` frames @ `24fps`, `1280\u00d7720`) foraged-plate + split-pin cutout film (`films/portholes/p13.mp4`) and live 60fps playable rig (`window.PORTAL_REMAKE_SCENES[13]`) in the authentic BOLAS Oulipo Screening Room aesthetic (`cardboard-parallax`, inspired by `la-mort-en-ce-jardin.webp (Luis Bu\u00f1uel & Queneau \u00b7 1956)`).\n\n## 2. Creative Thesis\n\u201cForaged or handmade, never faked.\u201d Use one line as the hinge that flips an argument. L\u00e9croart hinge on monochrome creek plates: suspend the foraged brass bell cutout beneath five silver-gelatin boulder planes as grey-cardboard swimmers test tripwire dinner bell, ferry doorbell, and stargate chime.\nRostrum Materiality (`cardboard-parallax`): Five parallax planes of monochrome/sepia botanical & river plate cutouts paired with mottled grey-cardboard jointed puppets, charcoal hatch marks, and glinting metallic split-pin brads.\n\n## 3. Active SCION Swarm Stack (4 Swarms + 2 Real Plates)\n- **Foraged Plates:** `./portholes/p13.jpg` + `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-54.webp` (Trading on the Current \u00b7 Bell by the fish. A fish and a small brass bell share the near view above a stony bottom.), preloaded via `SCION_STAGE.preloadPortalPlates(13)` and sliced via `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`.\n1. **Ouxpo / Oulipo Workshop SCION \u2014 Boucle-l\u00e0 ! (A short palindrome with a hinge):** \u00c9tienne L\u00e9croart \u00b7 Oubapo. Rule: Use one line as the hinge that flips an argument. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/boucle-la/)\n2. **Director / Artistic Lineage Swarm \u2014 S02 Lotte Reiniger \u2014 Articulated Shadow Theater:** 1920s silhouette puppets, hinged limbs, glass-table exposure. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s2)\n3. **Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Tech Swarms:**\n   - **S48 State Machines \u2014 Characters That Can Refuse:** Clockwise ferry-etiquette split-pin state machine (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s48)\n   - **S47 Sound-to-Action \u2014 Viseme and Gesture Swarm:** Foraged brass twig-bell cutout synced to Murbach chime (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s47)\n   - **S41 Secondary Dynamics \u2014 Inertia and Restraint Swarm:** 5 monochrome boulder-arch & ripple planes (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s41)\n4. **Turkey Sub World Atlas SCION \u2014 Trading on the Current (`#film-vVSDK8Z54Zs`):** \u201cLet the other fish confirm the handoff\u201d (./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-vVSDK8Z54Zs)\n\n## 4. 4-Beat Cutaway Invariants (A\u00b7B\u00b7C\u00b7D \u00b7 16.0s + Snail Mail)\n- **Variation I (`0.0\u20134.0s` \u00b7 A \u00b7 Real Creek \u00b7 `#14110d`):** Stage **\u201cA brass twig-bell on a rock\u201d** from scissor-cut real plate fragments and torn-paper flats.\n- **Variation II (`4.0\u20138.0s` \u00b7 B \u00b7 Probable (Turkey) \u00b7 `#1d596e`):** Rostrum shutter cut! Reframe the silhouette with split-pin cardboard/litho pieces into **\u201cA sneaky tripwire dinner bell\u201d** as Turkey\u2019s wing dispatches the **Mail Snail** with a wax-sealed postcard.\n- **Variation III (`8.0\u201312.0s` \u00b7 C \u00b7 Plausible (Trout) \u00b7 `#0f8f80`):** Creek witness cut! Brook the Trout inspects the scene reframed as **\u201cA polite creek ferry doorbell\u201d**, stamping the green reply as Mail Snail climbs the right edge.\n- **Variation IV (`12.0\u201316.0s` \u00b7 D \u00b7 Preposterous (Alien) \u00b7 `#d42a1e`):** Cosmic listening-post cut! The 3-eyed **Alien Listener** saucer scans and re-stages the cutouts into **\u201cA cosmic stargate toll chime\u201d**.\n\n## 5. Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Rig\n- Combine `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`, `SCION_STAGE.drawTornPaperFlat`, `SCION_STAGE.drawCardboardPuppetPiece`, `SCION_STAGE.drawSplitPin`, `SCION_STAGE.solveIK2`, and `SCION_STAGE.spring`.\n- Bind interactive 60fps state: `state.lamp`, `state.ballast`, `state.snailActive`/`state.snailT`, `state.roll` (1\u20136 die pips), and `state.view` (`\"real\" | \"turkey\" | \"trout\" | \"alien\" | \"auto\"`).\n- Mix 16.0s 44.1kHz stereo audio: dry spoken art-house variation cues (`Daniel` @ -16 dBFS) + paper slide, scissor snip, split-pin creak, postal bell, water lap, and Beat IV listening-post tone (`RMS > 0.025`).\n\n## 6. Hard Proof (16.0s / 384f)\n- Render `films/portholes/p13.mp4` (`1280x720`, `24fps`, `384` frames, `-crf 22`, AAC stereo), blind poster `thumbs/p13-remake.jpg` (`t = 2.2s`, `showCaptions: false`), and 4-column strip `checks/p13-remake-strip.jpg` (`2.0s, 6.0s, 10.0s, 14.0s`).\n- Provenance summary (9 sources): A 16.0-second (384-frame) four-variation cutout film in the Split-Pin Cardboard & Silver-Gelatin Parallax register, after TROUTOWN Ep. 3 (Trading on the Current) and Boucle-l\u00e0 ! (\u00c9tienne L\u00e9croart \u00b7 Oubapo). Foraged: porthole plate ./portholes/p13.jpg and Interior Atlas frame ./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-54.webp (\u201cTrading on the Current \u00b7 Bell by the fish. A fish and a small brass bell share the near view above a stony bottom.\u201d), sliced in code into irregular scissor-halo cutouts and multiplane depth cards\u2014never shown as a flat full-frame slide. Handmade: articulated grey-cardboard and deckle-paper pieces with metallic split-pin brads (S48/S47), staging all four student readings\u2014(A) \u201cA brass twig-bell on a rock\u201d, (B) \u201cA sneaky tripwire dinner bell\u201d with Snail Mail dispatch, (C) \u201cA polite creek ferry doorbell\u201d with Brook Trout's reply, and (D) \u201cA cosmic stargate toll chime\u201d under the Alien Listening Post. Sound: dry documentary voiceover (Daniel, -16 dBFS) paired with synthesized paper rustle, split-pin creak, brass postal chime, river lap, and listening-post tone, with declared quiet intervals between cuts.\n\n## 7. Blind Critic Fixture\n- **PAELEO Hard Invariant:** When `state.showCaptions === false`, emit **ZERO** `ctx.fillText` or `ctx.strokeText` calls anywhere (`0` leaked characters). Delegate all captions and the 4-box contact filmstrip to `SCION_STAGE.drawBolasSlateAndStrip` / `SCION_STAGE.drawRubricBar`.\n- Independent critic inspects `checks/p13-remake-strip.jpg` against `/tmp/bolas_refs/*.webp` and `./portholes/p13.jpg` to verify tactile cut-paper/cardboard/lithograph craft and distinct 4-beat visual transformations.\n\n## 8. Repair Loop\n- Reject flat untextured cartoon shapes or static Ken-Burns slides; re-cut plate fragments into articulated multi-plane pieces with visible paper halos, charcoal shading, and split-pin joints.\n\n## 9. Source Anchors\n- Porthole Plate: `./portholes/p13.jpg` \u00b7 Atlas Still: `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-54.webp` ([source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vVSDK8Z54Zs&t=40s))\n- BOLAS Screening Room: [Oulipo Screening Room](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/screening/)\n- Workshop SCION: [Boucle-l\u00e0 !](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/boucle-la/) \u00b7 Director Swarm: [S02 Lotte Reiniger \u2014 Articulated Shadow Theater](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s2)\n- Tech Swarms: [S48](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s48) \u00b7 [S47](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s47) \u00b7 [S41](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s41) \u00b7 Atlas: [Trading on the Current](./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-vVSDK8Z54Zs)",
    "compiledPromptPoml": ""
