    "compiledPromptMd": "# SCION MULTI-SWARM \u00b7 #18 (#18 \u00b7 Vent \u2014 Steamer trunk with star cutout peephole)\n\nLineage: The Shins: The Rifle\u2019s Spiral (2012) \u00b7 BOLAS Register: `perec-stage` (Carved Paper Proscenium & Tinted Archive) \u00b7 Workshop: 99 Ways to Tell a Story \u00b7 Subjective \u00b7 Director Swarm: S02 Lotte Reiniger \u2014 Articulated Shadow Theater.\n\n## 1. Assignment\nYou are the coordinated 4-SCION autonomous rostrum crew for Turkey Sub Porthole #18 \u00b7 Vent (\u201cSteamer trunk with star cutout peephole\u201d). Produce a 16.0-second (`384` frames @ `24fps`, `1280\u00d7720`) foraged-plate + split-pin cutout film (`films/portholes/p18.mp4`) and live 60fps playable rig (`window.PORTAL_REMAKE_SCENES[18]`) in the authentic BOLAS Oulipo Screening Room aesthetic (`perec-stage`, inspired by `les-lieux-dune-fugue.webp (Georges Perec \u00b7 1978)`).\n\n## 2. Creative Thesis\n\u201cForaged or handmade, never faked.\u201d Retell the same incident through what one participant can perceive. Rifle's Spiral carved trunk stage: swing open a relief-shaded paper trunk lid with a 5-point star cutout onto a starry archival plate\u2014retold as steamer trunk, pirate chest, trick box, and pocket constellation.\nRostrum Materiality (`perec-stage`): Carved sandstone/ochre paper masonry proscenium with relief shadows and hinged paper shutters opening onto cool cyanotype/sepia archival plates.\n\n## 3. Active SCION Swarm Stack (4 Swarms + 2 Real Plates)\n- **Foraged Plates:** `./portholes/p18.jpg` + `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-38.webp` (The Rifle\u2019s Spiral \u00b7 Hinged miniature. A hinged dark lid becomes a tiny stage with stars and crescent cut shapes.), preloaded via `SCION_STAGE.preloadPortalPlates(18)` and sliced via `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`.\n1. **Ouxpo / Oulipo Workshop SCION \u2014 99 Ways to Tell a Story \u00b7 Subjective (First-person reconstruction):** Matt Madden \u00b7 2005. Rule: Retell the same incident through what one participant can perceive. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/99-ways-subjective/)\n2. **Director / Artistic Lineage Swarm \u2014 S02 Lotte Reiniger \u2014 Articulated Shadow Theater:** 1920s silhouette puppets, hinged limbs, glass-table exposure. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s2)\n3. **Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Tech Swarms:**\n   - **S32 Forward Kinematics \u2014 Hierarchical Body Logic:** Hinged paper steamer-trunk lid & star aperture FK (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s32)\n   - **S45 Occlusion Compositing \u2014 Who Is In Front?:** Star peephole masking Rifle's Spiral starlight plate (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s45)\n   - **S44 Multiplane Parallax \u2014 Spatial Collage Swarm:** Deep pocket-constellation parallax recess (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s44)\n4. **Turkey Sub World Atlas SCION \u2014 The Rifle\u2019s Spiral (`#film-jyqWjl7GkCE`):** \u201cLet a hinge bear weight\u201d (./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-jyqWjl7GkCE)\n\n## 4. 4-Beat Cutaway Invariants (A\u00b7B\u00b7C\u00b7D \u00b7 16.0s + Snail Mail)\n- **Variation I (`0.0\u20134.0s` \u00b7 A \u00b7 Real Creek \u00b7 `#14110d`):** Stage **\u201cA star-carved old steamer trunk\u201d** from scissor-cut real plate fragments and torn-paper flats.\n- **Variation II (`4.0\u20138.0s` \u00b7 B \u00b7 Probable (Turkey) \u00b7 `#1d596e`):** Rostrum shutter cut! Reframe the silhouette with split-pin cardboard/litho pieces into **\u201cA sunken pirate treasure chest\u201d** as Turkey\u2019s wing dispatches the **Mail Snail** with a wax-sealed postcard.\n- **Variation III (`8.0\u201312.0s` \u00b7 C \u00b7 Plausible (Trout) \u00b7 `#0f8f80`):** Creek witness cut! Brook the Trout inspects the scene reframed as **\u201cA stage magician\u2019s trick box\u201d**, stamping the green reply as Mail Snail climbs the right edge.\n- **Variation IV (`12.0\u201316.0s` \u00b7 D \u00b7 Preposterous (Alien) \u00b7 `#d42a1e`):** Cosmic listening-post cut! The 3-eyed **Alien Listener** saucer scans and re-stages the cutouts into **\u201cA trapped pocket constellation\u201d**.\n\n## 5. Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Rig\n- Combine `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`, `SCION_STAGE.drawTornPaperFlat`, `SCION_STAGE.drawCardboardPuppetPiece`, `SCION_STAGE.drawSplitPin`, `SCION_STAGE.solveIK2`, and `SCION_STAGE.spring`.\n- Bind interactive 60fps state: `state.lamp`, `state.ballast`, `state.snailActive`/`state.snailT`, `state.roll` (1\u20136 die pips), and `state.view` (`\"real\" | \"turkey\" | \"trout\" | \"alien\" | \"auto\"`).\n- Mix 16.0s 44.1kHz stereo audio: dry spoken art-house variation cues (`Rishi` @ -16 dBFS) + paper slide, scissor snip, split-pin creak, postal bell, water lap, and Beat IV listening-post tone (`RMS > 0.025`).\n\n## 6. Hard Proof (16.0s / 384f)\n- Render `films/portholes/p18.mp4` (`1280x720`, `24fps`, `384` frames, `-crf 22`, AAC stereo), blind poster `thumbs/p18-remake.jpg` (`t = 2.2s`, `showCaptions: false`), and 4-column strip `checks/p18-remake-strip.jpg` (`2.0s, 6.0s, 10.0s, 14.0s`).\n- Provenance summary (9 sources): A 16.0-second (384-frame) four-variation cutout film in the Carved Paper Proscenium & Tinted Archive register, after The Shins: The Rifle\u2019s Spiral (2012) and 99 Ways to Tell a Story \u00b7 Subjective (Matt Madden \u00b7 2005). Foraged: porthole plate ./portholes/p18.jpg and Interior Atlas frame ./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-38.webp (\u201cThe Rifle\u2019s Spiral \u00b7 Hinged miniature. A hinged dark lid becomes a tiny stage with stars and crescent cut shapes.\u201d), sliced in code into irregular scissor-halo cutouts and multiplane depth cards\u2014never shown as a flat full-frame slide. Handmade: articulated grey-cardboard and deckle-paper pieces with metallic split-pin brads (S32/S45), staging all four student readings\u2014(A) \u201cA star-carved old steamer trunk\u201d, (B) \u201cA sunken pirate treasure chest\u201d with Snail Mail dispatch, (C) \u201cA stage magician\u2019s trick box\u201d with Brook Trout's reply, and (D) \u201cA trapped pocket constellation\u201d under the Alien Listening Post. Sound: dry documentary voiceover (Rishi, -16 dBFS) paired with synthesized paper rustle, split-pin creak, brass postal chime, river lap, and listening-post tone, with declared quiet intervals between cuts.\n\n## 7. Blind Critic Fixture\n- **PAELEO Hard Invariant:** When `state.showCaptions === false`, emit **ZERO** `ctx.fillText` or `ctx.strokeText` calls anywhere (`0` leaked characters). Delegate all captions and the 4-box contact filmstrip to `SCION_STAGE.drawBolasSlateAndStrip` / `SCION_STAGE.drawRubricBar`.\n- Independent critic inspects `checks/p18-remake-strip.jpg` against `/tmp/bolas_refs/*.webp` and `./portholes/p18.jpg` to verify tactile cut-paper/cardboard/lithograph craft and distinct 4-beat visual transformations.\n\n## 8. Repair Loop\n- Reject flat untextured cartoon shapes or static Ken-Burns slides; re-cut plate fragments into articulated multi-plane pieces with visible paper halos, charcoal shading, and split-pin joints.\n\n## 9. Source Anchors\n- Porthole Plate: `./portholes/p18.jpg` \u00b7 Atlas Still: `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-38.webp` ([source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jyqWjl7GkCE&t=82s))\n- BOLAS Screening Room: [Oulipo Screening Room](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/screening/)\n- Workshop SCION: [99 Ways to Tell a Story \u00b7 Subjective](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/99-ways-subjective/) \u00b7 Director Swarm: [S02 Lotte Reiniger \u2014 Articulated Shadow Theater](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s2)\n- Tech Swarms: [S32](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s32) \u00b7 [S45](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s45) \u00b7 [S44](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s44) \u00b7 Atlas: [The Rifle\u2019s Spiral](./scion-interior-atlas.html#film-jyqWjl7GkCE)",
    "compiledPromptPoml": ""
