    "compiledPromptMd": "# SCION MULTI-SWARM \u00b7 #19 (#19 \u00b7 Bilge \u2014 Raw potato skewered with 10 bendy straws)\n\nLineage: PAE-09 Lab \u00b7 Calvino: Cosmicomics \u00b7 BOLAS Register: `duchamp-optic` (Engraved Rotor, Paper-Tooth & Reverse-Melt Slate) \u00b7 Workshop: Bang Bang \u00b7 Director Swarm: S09 Takeo Igarashi \u2014 As-Rigid-as-Possible Puppetry.\n\n## 1. Assignment\nYou are the coordinated 4-SCION autonomous rostrum crew for Turkey Sub Porthole #19 \u00b7 Bilge (\u201cRaw potato skewered with 10 bendy straws\u201d). Produce a 16.0-second (`384` frames @ `24fps`, `1280\u00d7720`) foraged-plate + split-pin cutout film (`films/portholes/p19.mp4`) and live 60fps playable rig (`window.PORTAL_REMAKE_SCENES[19]`) in the authentic BOLAS Oulipo Screening Room aesthetic (`duchamp-optic`, inspired by `anemic-cinema / zazie-dans-le-metro / le-chant-du-styrene`).\n\n## 2. Creative Thesis\n\u201cForaged or handmade, never faked.\u201d Build a story from the friction between a witness and the machinery it observes. Bang-Bang apparatus slate: pin ten jointed paper bendy-straws with metallic brads onto a foraged potato cutout over dark workshop slate\u2014becoming sea urchin, potato-eating creek bug, and ten-antennaed satellite.\nRostrum Materiality (`duchamp-optic`): Dark workshop slate stage featuring eccentric engraved optical discs, physical cut-paper block typography/props, or reverse-extrusion runner cutouts with cream scissor halos.\n\n## 3. Active SCION Swarm Stack (4 Swarms + 2 Real Plates)\n- **Foraged Plates:** `./portholes/p19.jpg` + `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-35.webp` (Water Fountain \u00b7 Object as display. A small CRT with visible external wires holds a bold, simple house graphic.), preloaded via `SCION_STAGE.preloadPortalPlates(19)` and sliced via `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`.\n1. **Ouxpo / Oulipo Workshop SCION \u2014 Bang Bang (An impossible narrator and a working storyboard):** Jean Jabely and Raymond Queneau \u00b7 c. 1958 dossier. Rule: Build a story from the friction between a witness and the machinery it observes. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/bang-bang/)\n2. **Director / Artistic Lineage Swarm \u2014 S09 Takeo Igarashi \u2014 As-Rigid-as-Possible Puppetry:** As-rigid-as-possible shape manipulation, 2005. (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s9)\n3. **Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Tech Swarms:**\n   - **S34 ARAP \u2014 Preserve-Shape Deformation Swarm:** Scissor-cut raw potato plate crop at center (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s34)\n   - **S41 Secondary Dynamics \u2014 Inertia and Restraint Swarm:** 10 split-pin paper bendy-straw cantilevers (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s41)\n   - **S32 Forward Kinematics \u2014 Hierarchical Body Logic:** Sputnik orbital spin & antenna ping (https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s32)\n4. **Turkey Sub World Atlas SCION \u2014 Trade a spent cell (`#verne-01`):** \u201cMake power a cause that gives the pilot a destination. Introduce a toy cell with two visible marks and a charger at the Works. Give one task one spent mark. The shore route can still be walked.\u201d (./scion-interior-atlas.html#verne-01)\n\n## 4. 4-Beat Cutaway Invariants (A\u00b7B\u00b7C\u00b7D \u00b7 16.0s + Snail Mail)\n- **Variation I (`0.0\u20134.0s` \u00b7 A \u00b7 Real Creek \u00b7 `#14110d`):** Stage **\u201cA potato poked with bendy straws\u201d** from scissor-cut real plate fragments and torn-paper flats.\n- **Variation II (`4.0\u20138.0s` \u00b7 B \u00b7 Probable (Turkey) \u00b7 `#1d596e`):** Rostrum shutter cut! Reframe the silhouette with split-pin cardboard/litho pieces into **\u201cA giant spiky sea urchin\u201d** as Turkey\u2019s wing dispatches the **Mail Snail** with a wax-sealed postcard.\n- **Variation III (`8.0\u201312.0s` \u00b7 C \u00b7 Plausible (Trout) \u00b7 `#0f8f80`):** Creek witness cut! Brook the Trout inspects the scene reframed as **\u201cA sneaky potato-eating creek bug\u201d**, stamping the green reply as Mail Snail climbs the right edge.\n- **Variation IV (`12.0\u201316.0s` \u00b7 D \u00b7 Preposterous (Alien) \u00b7 `#d42a1e`):** Cosmic listening-post cut! The 3-eyed **Alien Listener** saucer scans and re-stages the cutouts into **\u201cA ten-antennaed potato satellite\u201d**.\n\n## 5. Kinematics, Parallax & Sound Rig\n- Combine `SCION_STAGE.drawScissorCutout`, `SCION_STAGE.drawTornPaperFlat`, `SCION_STAGE.drawCardboardPuppetPiece`, `SCION_STAGE.drawSplitPin`, `SCION_STAGE.solveIK2`, and `SCION_STAGE.spring`.\n- Bind interactive 60fps state: `state.lamp`, `state.ballast`, `state.snailActive`/`state.snailT`, `state.roll` (1\u20136 die pips), and `state.view` (`\"real\" | \"turkey\" | \"trout\" | \"alien\" | \"auto\"`).\n- Mix 16.0s 44.1kHz stereo audio: dry spoken art-house variation cues (`Daniel` @ -16 dBFS) + paper slide, scissor snip, split-pin creak, postal bell, water lap, and Beat IV listening-post tone (`RMS > 0.025`).\n\n## 6. Hard Proof (16.0s / 384f)\n- Render `films/portholes/p19.mp4` (`1280x720`, `24fps`, `384` frames, `-crf 22`, AAC stereo), blind poster `thumbs/p19-remake.jpg` (`t = 2.2s`, `showCaptions: false`), and 4-column strip `checks/p19-remake-strip.jpg` (`2.0s, 6.0s, 10.0s, 14.0s`).\n- Provenance summary (9 sources): A 16.0-second (384-frame) four-variation cutout film in the Engraved Rotor, Paper-Tooth & Reverse-Melt Slate register, after PAE-09 Lab \u00b7 Calvino: Cosmicomics and Bang Bang (Jean Jabely and Raymond Queneau \u00b7 c. 1958 dossier). Foraged: porthole plate ./portholes/p19.jpg and Interior Atlas frame ./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-35.webp (\u201cWater Fountain \u00b7 Object as display. A small CRT with visible external wires holds a bold, simple house graphic.\u201d), sliced in code into irregular scissor-halo cutouts and multiplane depth cards\u2014never shown as a flat full-frame slide. Handmade: articulated grey-cardboard and deckle-paper pieces with metallic split-pin brads (S34/S41), staging all four student readings\u2014(A) \u201cA potato poked with bendy straws\u201d, (B) \u201cA giant spiky sea urchin\u201d with Snail Mail dispatch, (C) \u201cA sneaky potato-eating creek bug\u201d with Brook Trout's reply, and (D) \u201cA ten-antennaed potato satellite\u201d under the Alien Listening Post. Sound: dry documentary voiceover (Daniel, -16 dBFS) paired with synthesized paper rustle, split-pin creak, brass postal chime, river lap, and listening-post tone, with declared quiet intervals between cuts.\n\n## 7. Blind Critic Fixture\n- **PAELEO Hard Invariant:** When `state.showCaptions === false`, emit **ZERO** `ctx.fillText` or `ctx.strokeText` calls anywhere (`0` leaked characters). Delegate all captions and the 4-box contact filmstrip to `SCION_STAGE.drawBolasSlateAndStrip` / `SCION_STAGE.drawRubricBar`.\n- Independent critic inspects `checks/p19-remake-strip.jpg` against `/tmp/bolas_refs/*.webp` and `./portholes/p19.jpg` to verify tactile cut-paper/cardboard/lithograph craft and distinct 4-beat visual transformations.\n\n## 8. Repair Loop\n- Reject flat untextured cartoon shapes or static Ken-Burns slides; re-cut plate fragments into articulated multi-plane pieces with visible paper halos, charcoal shading, and split-pin joints.\n\n## 9. Source Anchors\n- Porthole Plate: `./portholes/p19.jpg` \u00b7 Atlas Still: `./assets/atlas-stills/atlas-35.webp` ([source](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jbiFcPhccu8&t=68s))\n- BOLAS Screening Room: [Oulipo Screening Room](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/screening/)\n- Workshop SCION: [Bang Bang](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/oulipo/s/bang-bang/) \u00b7 Director Swarm: [S09 Takeo Igarashi \u2014 As-Rigid-as-Possible Puppetry](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s9)\n- Tech Swarms: [S34](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s34) \u00b7 [S41](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s41) \u00b7 [S32](https://hartswf0.github.io/bolas/paeleo/scion/operator.html#s32) \u00b7 Atlas: [Trade a spent cell](./scion-interior-atlas.html#verne-01)",
    "compiledPromptPoml": ""
